@startuml Fault Detection Participant Diagram
title Figure X: Fault Detection & Diagnostic Scan Participant Diagram

' Professional Sequence Diagram Styling
skinparam actorStyle awesome
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam handwritten false
skinparam monochrome false
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam ParticipantPadding 40
skinparam BoxPadding 10

skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #0078d4
    LifeLineBorderColor #0078d4
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #f0f7ff
    
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #f0f7ff
    ParticipantBorderColor #0078d4
    ParticipantFontSize 14
    ParticipantFontColor #0078d4
    
    ActorBackgroundColor #f0f7ff
    ActorBorderColor #0078d4
}

skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #fff9e6
    BorderColor #d4a017
    FontSize 11
}

actor "Plant Operator" as User
participant "FaultDetection UI" as UI <<Boundary>>
participant "Diagnostic Engine" as Engine <<Control>>
participant "AI Model API" as AI <<External Service>>
database "Supabase" as DB <<Database>>

autonumber

User -> UI : Click "Run Full Diagnostics Scan"
activate UI

UI -> Engine : runDiagnostics()
activate Engine

loop for each subsystem (Compressor, Condenser, Sensors)
    Engine -> AI : Analyze sensor patterns (POST features)
    activate AI
    AI --> Engine : Anomaly Score & Failure Probability
    deactivate AI
    
    Engine -> Engine : Evaluate against thresholds
end

Engine --> UI : Diagnostic Results (List of Alerts)
deactivate Engine

UI -> UI : Update Local State (faults)
UI -> UI : showToast("Scan Complete")

UI --> User : Display New Alerts & Health Scores
deactivate UI

note right of Engine
  **Pattern Recognition:**
  The engine uses the AI Model
  to differentiate between
  normal operational noise
  and actual mechanical faults.
end note

@enduml
